    "created_at": "2026-08-06T10:31:55Z",
    "updated_at": "2026-08-06T10:33:31Z",
    "body": "> The spec says yes\n\nDoes it?\n\n- [`show a modal dialog`](https://html.spec.whatwg.org/#show-a-modal-dialog) step 18 - `hideUntil` becomes the `hint` popover\n- step 19 - [`hide all popovers until`](https://html.spec.whatwg.org/#hide-popovers-until) with said hint as `endpoint`\n- step 1 - sets `endpointIsHint` to `true`.\n- step 2 - All other hint popovers hide....\n- step 3 - if `endpointIsHint == true` then return.\n\nSo I think the unrelated auto _doesn't_ hide. \n\nWhether or not it should is perhaps a separate matter. I don't have a strong opinion as it's a very edge case. ",
